  "description": "Keane Thompson are delighted to present this well-positioned one-bedroom, one-bathroom apartment to the rental market in Hyde Square, Dublin 8.\n\nThe apartment comprises a bright open-plan living and kitchen area, a well-proportioned double bedroom, modern bathroom and a large storage room, providing excellent additional storage space. The property also benefits from a west-facing balcony, ideal for enjoying the afternoon and evening sun.\n\nHyde Square is a popular residential development located just off the South Circular Road, offering an excellent combination of convenient city living and a wide range of amenities on the doorstep.\n\nThe surrounding area has an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars, supermarkets and local shops. Dublin 8 is also home to some of the city's most popular attractions, including Kilmainham Gaol, the Guinness Storehouse, the Irish Museum of Modern Art (IMMA) and the Royal Hospital Kilmainham.\n\nTransport links are excellent, with the Luas Red Line within walking distance, providing easy access to Dublin City Centre, Heuston Station, Tallaght and Saggart. There are also numerous Dublin Bus routes operating in the surrounding area. Heuston Station is close by, providing rail and intercity connections.\n\nThe location is particularly convenient for accessibility to the city centre which is easily accessible by public transport, bicycle or on foot. The property also offers convenient access to the South Circular Road and the M50 for commuters travelling further afield.\n\nAnyone looking to enjoy the outdoors, Phoenix Park is within easy reach, while the area also benefits from a number of local parks and recreational facilities.\n\nPlease note there is no parking with this apartment.\n\nProperty Features:\n\n1 double bedroom\n1 bathroom\nBright open-plan living and kitchen area\nWest-facing balcony\nLarge storage room\nExcellent Dublin 8 location\nLuas Red Line within walking distance\nClose to Heuston Station\nExcellent Dublin Bus connections\nEasy access to Dublin City Centre and the M50\nClose to a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants and bars",
